1089 "q-100482" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251266 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533789 true] [17592186251266 1100 "Find the solution of ${4}^{x+7}={5}^{8-4x}.$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251266 1113 #uuid "386df23c-8f42-53d4-b137-e274cd1470c7" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251266 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{x+7} & ={5}^{8-4x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{x+7}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{8-4x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify both sides of the equation. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) & =(8-4x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) & =(8-4x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) & =8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) & =8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)) & =8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) \\\\ x & =\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251268 13194139533789 true] [17592186251267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251269 13194139533789 true] [17592186251267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251270 13194139533789 true] [17592186251267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251271 13194139533789 true] [17592186251267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251272 13194139533789 true] [17592186251267 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533789 true] [17592186251267 1041 "selection" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251267 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251272 13194139533789 true] [17592186251267 1110 #uuid "d2283c37-fc3d-5c24-b59a-65e299a2cd14" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251268 1034 "-\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251268 1111 #uuid "cf8e4434-1802-5c8e-be31-df2b56fba857" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251269 1034 "\\frac{1}{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251269 1111 #uuid "2c37f8d7-1d47-5d1d-a8cc-1e51da99f877" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251270 1034 "\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251270 1111 #uuid "55f0cc8f-4beb-5dc5-81ef-3d5b824e306e" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251271 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251271 1111 #uuid "bbfc6fac-cdab-5eb8-85fe-89d2a89c6a26" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251272 1034 "\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251272 1111 #uuid "c539139d-2c41-58be-b2fc-7910e236a7fc" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251273 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251274 13194139533789 true] [17592186251273 1089 "q-110545" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251273 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533789 true] [17592186251273 1100 "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, what value of $y$ satisfies the equation ${e}^{y}={8}^{1-2y}?$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251273 1113 #uuid "47457fc5-4715-5250-8afb-4edbb48c0413" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251273 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y} & ={8}^{1-2y} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({8}^{1-2y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({8}^{1-2y})\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\ny=(1-2y)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(1-2y)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)-2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ y+2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ y(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}{1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251275 13194139533789 true] [17592186251274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251276 13194139533789 true] [17592186251274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251277 13194139533789 true] [17592186251274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251278 13194139533789 true] [17592186251274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251279 13194139533789 true] [17592186251274 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533789 true] [17592186251274 1041 "selection" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251274 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251275 13194139533789 true] [17592186251274 1110 #uuid "2e6162b3-6a3d-59f3-87d1-504aa5c92d11" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251275 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}{1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251275 1111 #uuid "0fcaebca-cab8-533b-8890-7b9e1f628c87" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251276 1034 "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251276 1111 #uuid "0c792d3e-7096-5d22-b213-f53e91a6409d" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251277 1034 "\\frac{1}{2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251277 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251277 1111 #uuid "988dc7fb-e0a5-5faa-b378-00b15774a54d" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251278 1034 "1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251278 1111 #uuid "0d1e9b47-3151-5f52-a03d-a411a0b05931" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251279 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251279 1111 #uuid "203dd4eb-be6e-59cd-add0-497d7e174b05" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251280 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251281 13194139533789 true] [17592186251280 1089 "q-242899" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251280 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533789 true] [17592186251280 1100 "Given that ${8}^{1-x}={3}^{x/2},$ what is the value of $x?$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251280 1113 #uuid "9fbe8518-3b94-57e7-a090-a9853e4fce38" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251280 1145 "First, we take ${log}_{8}$ on both sides of the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{1-x} & ={3}^{x/2} \\\\ {log}_{8}⁡({8}^{1-x}) & ={log}_{8}⁡({3}^{x/2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n1-x={log}_{8}⁡({3}^{x/2})\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n1-x=\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}⁡3\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-x & =\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}⁡3 \\\\ 1 & =x+\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}⁡3 \\\\ x+\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}⁡3 & =1 \\\\ 2x+x{log}_{8}⁡3 & =2 \\\\ x(2+{log}_{8}⁡3) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{2+{log}_{8}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the change of base formula, we have\n\n$$\n{log}_{8}⁡(3)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}≈0.528\\,321.\n$$\n\nFinally,  we can approximate $x$ as \n\n$$\nx≈\\frac{2}{2+0.528\\,321}≈0.791,\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533789 true] [17592186251281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251282 13194139533789 true] [17592186251281 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533789 true] [17592186251281 1041 "field-1" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251281 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251282 13194139533789 true] [17592186251281 1110 #uuid "2b1bdacb-07a0-5d62-a827-f3d945513621" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251282 1034 "0.791" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251282 1111 #uuid "b87f1ee2-1ef7-5b1c-b22c-96427b594c17" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251283 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251284 13194139533789 true] [17592186251283 1089 "q-242903" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251283 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533789 true] [17592186251283 1100 "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${e}^{3x-1}={6}^{2x+1}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251283 1113 #uuid "9c85f3bb-5b0c-5344-bb83-aedc5a84595c" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251283 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3x-1} & ={6}^{2x+1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3x-1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({6}^{2x+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n3x-1=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({6}^{2x+1}).\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n3x-1=(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-1 & =(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6) \\\\ 3x-1 & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6) \\\\ 3x-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6) & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6) \\\\ x(3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)) & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}{3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251285 13194139533789 true] [17592186251284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251286 13194139533789 true] [17592186251284 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533789 true] [17592186251284 1041 "field-1" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251284 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251285 13194139533789 true] [17592186251284 1110 #uuid "938a59ad-4ed3-5929-8558-874207b631aa" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251285 1034 "\\frac{1+\\ln(6)}{3-2\\ln(6)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251285 1111 #uuid "715a26cb-ec55-5a22-ba50-cd6081ec7ee6" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251286 1034 "\\frac{1+\\ln(6)}{3+2\\ln(6)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251286 1111 #uuid "05cb3666-b42d-5153-a1bc-adb70cc644b5" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251287 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251288 13194139533789 true] [17592186251287 1089 "q-242906" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251287 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533789 true] [17592186251287 1100 "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${e}^{x-2}={10}^{-3x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251287 1113 #uuid "48d8d194-845b-5ebe-96aa-f1c5bae21aa9" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251287 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-2} & ={10}^{-3x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x-2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({10}^{-3x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx-2=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({10}^{-3x}).\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nx-2=-3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2 & =-3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\ x+3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) & =2 \\\\ x(1+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{1+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251289 13194139533789 true] [17592186251288 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533789 true] [17592186251288 1041 "field-1" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251288 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251289 13194139533789 true] [17592186251288 1110 #uuid "29387e85-e297-562f-a5f3-bddfca71e012" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251289 1034 "\\frac{2}{1+3\\ln(10)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251289 1111 #uuid "2472b62e-532d-532c-bdd9-8bf800d61936" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251290 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251291 13194139533789 true] [17592186251290 1089 "q-242918" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251290 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533789 true] [17592186251290 1100 "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${8}^{2x}={10}^{x-7}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251290 1113 #uuid "5f0395a0-8645-5c1d-b942-d51d175720a8" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251290 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{2x} & ={10}^{x-7} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({8}^{2x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({10}^{x-7})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify both sides of the equation. This gives\n\n$$\n2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)=(x-7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) & =(x-7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) & =-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) & =7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)) & =7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\ x & =\\frac{7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251292 13194139533789 true] [17592186251291 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533789 true] [17592186251291 1041 "field-1" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251291 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251292 13194139533789 true] [17592186251291 1110 #uuid "8920f265-8ec3-596e-9dfb-4e308a1fba6c" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251292 1034 "\\frac{7\\ln(10)}{\\ln(10)-2\\ln(8)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251292 1111 #uuid "e4d1e211-be1e-51cd-9f19-6da94007bb6b" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251293 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251294 13194139533789 true] [17592186251293 1089 "q-242923" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251293 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533789 true] [17592186251293 1100 "Find the solution of ${3}^{2x}={8}^{1-6x}.$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251293 1113 #uuid "e3b45ed9-d96c-5211-9aac-db609bef71c5" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251293 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2x} & ={8}^{1-6x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({8}^{1-6x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify both sides of the equation. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) & =(1-6x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) & =(1-6x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ 2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8))}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251295 13194139533789 true] [17592186251294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251296 13194139533789 true] [17592186251294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251297 13194139533789 true] [17592186251294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251298 13194139533789 true] [17592186251294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251299 13194139533789 true] [17592186251294 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533789 true] [17592186251294 1041 "selection" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251294 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251297 13194139533789 true] [17592186251294 1110 #uuid "f7c97278-8fd5-505c-8034-ecd7054e4203" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251295 1034 "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251295 1111 #uuid "cdb6db08-ce2e-5e89-ac1b-30cfe9f6e53f" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251296 1034 "\\frac{1}{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8))}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251296 1111 #uuid "926b8b59-0c00-560e-8af1-404e27725e61" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251297 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8))}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251297 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251297 1111 #uuid "ccd199d3-ff22-54b7-a8f3-88c6742eee51" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251298 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251298 1111 #uuid "4e1a0989-c177-578b-8f9a-c1dca813a14f" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251299 1034 "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251299 1111 #uuid "c61e310b-f791-5855-9987-ec6a564dca1e" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251300 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251301 13194139533789 true] [17592186251300 1089 "q-242938" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251300 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533789 true] [17592186251300 1100 "Expressed in terms of common logarithms, what value of $x$ satisfies the equation ${10}^{x+1}={2}^{x}?$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251300 1113 #uuid "a80e13c8-4b2d-570c-89d6-a9e588816f96" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251300 1145 "First, we take the common logarithm $(log)$ of both sides of the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{10}^{x+1} & ={2}^{x} \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x+1}) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({2}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+1=\\operatorname{log}⁡({2}^{x})\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nx+1=x\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)-x & =1 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)-1) & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251301 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251302 13194139533789 true] [17592186251301 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251303 13194139533789 true] [17592186251301 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533789 true] [17592186251301 1041 "field-1" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251301 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251303 13194139533789 true] [17592186251301 1110 #uuid "1d20689e-f160-5519-ba1e-e161d006fcd5" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251302 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\log(2)+1}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251302 1111 #uuid "a780f4a0-8450-5cb8-805a-2dd97752953c" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251303 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\log(2)-1}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251303 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251303 1111 #uuid "3dda0191-cfab-52a8-984d-da80f345ebf4" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251304 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251305 13194139533789 true] [17592186251304 1089 "q-26385" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251304 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533789 true] [17592186251304 1100 "Expressed in terms of common logarithms, what value of $x$ satisfies the equation ${10}^{x-3}={7}^{x}?$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251304 1113 #uuid "ed7ab01a-8bb8-585b-9681-7e499c6dc236" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251304 1145 "First, we take the common logarithm $(log)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{10}^{x-3} & ={7}^{x} \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x-3}) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({7}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({7}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & =x\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-x\\operatorname{log}⁡(7) & =3 \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)) & =3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{1-\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251306 13194139533789 true] [17592186251305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251307 13194139533789 true] [17592186251305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251308 13194139533789 true] [17592186251305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251309 13194139533789 true] [17592186251305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251310 13194139533789 true] [17592186251305 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533789 true] [17592186251305 1041 "selection" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251305 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251310 13194139533789 true] [17592186251305 1110 #uuid "49d093e8-d228-59bf-800a-810003a75896" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251306 1034 "1-\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251306 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251306 1111 #uuid "931a4ce6-7435-585c-9775-66d58253118b" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251307 1034 "\\frac{1}{1+2\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251307 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251307 1111 #uuid "50ba0cd1-2629-5afe-ab11-6821ac544fce" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251308 1034 "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251308 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251308 1111 #uuid "42f06250-b7c9-580a-9166-2cfbdac14d2a" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251309 1034 "-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251309 1111 #uuid "60d37d82-ee94-569c-aaf8-e1423aeb7f4b" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251310 1034 "\\frac{3}{1-\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533789 true] [17592186251310 1111 #uuid "a6df1250-c2da-5c4f-8078-44a8901d5507" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251311 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251312 13194139533789 true] [17592186251311 1089 "q-26828" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251311 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533789 true] [17592186251311 1100 "Given that ${5}^{y}={4}^{y+1},$ what is the value of $y?$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533789 true] [17592186251311 1113 #uuid "c1b384d1-bf1d-5185-800b-b0cf5436aeb1" 13194139533789 true] [17592186251311 1145 "First, we take ${log}_{5}$ on both sides of the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{y}={4}^{y+1} \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡({5}^{y}) & ={log}_{5}⁡({4}^{y+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={log}_{5}⁡({4}^{y+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(y+1){log}_{5}⁡4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(y+1){log}_{5}⁡4 \\\\ y & =y{log}_{5}⁡4+{log}_{5}⁡4 \\\\ y-y{log}_{5}⁡4 & ={log}_{5}⁡4 \\\\ y(1-{log}_{5}⁡4) & ={log}_{5}⁡4 \\\\ y & =\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡4}{1-{log}_{5}⁡4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the change of base formula, we have\n\n$$\n{log}_{5}⁡(4)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}≈0.861\\,353.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, we can approximate $y$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y≈\\frac{0.861\\,353}{1-0.861\\,353}≈6.213,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $3$ decimal places." 13194139533